================================================================================
Third-party software
================================================================================

yagura ships as a single statically-linked binary built from the Go standard
library only — no external Go module dependencies (see docs/adr/0001-zero-dependencies.md).

The Go standard library is licensed by The Go Authors under the BSD-3-Clause
license. See https://go.googlesource.com/go/+/refs/heads/master/LICENSE for the
full text.

================================================================================
Build & toolchain
================================================================================

Reproducible builds of yagura are produced with:

  - The Go compiler (BSD-3-Clause), version pinned per release.
  - GNU Make (GPL-3.0-or-later), used as a build front-end only; not redistributed.

These tools are used at build time and are not part of the distributed binary.

================================================================================
Inspiration & external references
================================================================================

Yagura draws design ideas from public engineering writing by Anthropic, OpenAI,
Martin Fowler / Thoughtworks, LangChain, and Mitchell Hashimoto. None of that
code is bundled here, but the work is gratefully acknowledged in README.md and
in individual ADRs under docs/adr/.
